      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "SpinDamp represents the difference between two Contact components, one on an undamped reference, one on a damped rotation constraint to that reference. The SpinDamp float is used to drive the “tightness” of its own damped rotation constraint; the bigger the difference between the two, the tighter/faster the damped rotation constraint gets. This keeps the two Contact components from ever getting too far apart from each other.\n\nI’m putting this comment here in case it’s relevant to the station reset behavior, but I also have recently been getting paradoxical behavior in another system driven by SpinDamp. Fullbody users will sometimes have constant hind leg stepping that never resolves (until they walk forward to reset their root rotation(?)), even though hind leg stepping is driven solely by SpinDamp, and should only ever represent a state that is actively resolving itself (if SpinDamp is past the point where stepping happens, the constraints should be tightened up enough to stop the stepping in less than a second). Instead fullbody users sometimes just stand there, with their hind legs constantly stepping… I never had this happen before iirc",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
